// lexdb_exec: the audit's wrong answers and wrong errors in the PostgreSQL door (design/lexdb-new-features.md: P10
// reverse(bytea), P12 to_number(text, 'RN'), P20 EXTRACT's column name, P21 IS DISTINCT FROM's, P22 0x/0o/0b and _
// in numbers and in text cast to integers, || of two numbers, an unknown function refused when bound, SUM and AVG of
// intervals), checked against PostgreSQL 18 (generated by tests/lexdb/gen_pg.py from newfix_queries.txt). Each
// answer: the columns' names and the rows, or the tag, or ERROR and the SQLSTATE; each query runs with lexdb_batch
// off and on: "same: " and the answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
